WEBVTT

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:03.970
<i>I will now explain the second program!</i>

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:07.180
<i>Five-on-five team battles!</i>

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:08.640
Team battles?

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.720
<i>We'll escort you to the venue in two hours.</i>

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:15.150
Huh? Is that all?

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:18.280
Briefer than the explanation 
we got for the one-on-ones.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:21.740
What am I supposed to do with 
these weirdos for two hours?

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.170
<i>I wasn't expecting this so soon.</i>

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.590
<i>Two hours...</i>

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.910
<i>I had guessed that if their goal 
was to make us kill each other,</i>

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:32.520
<i>group battles would be inevitable.</i>

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.480
<i>If we want to coordinate, we'll have 
to reveal our abilities to each other.</i>

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:40.220
<b><<Sophist>>

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:43.980
<i>My real ability is whatever the 
other person thinks my ability is,</i>

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.800
<i>and Kirisaki thinks mine is the cannon.</i>

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:52.440
<i>Should I tell my team my real ability?</i>

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:26.830
<b>Episode 3  "Trueblade"</b>

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:27.800
Guess we're in this one together, eh?

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:31.730
I say we use this time to get to know 
each other and cook up a plan!

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:32.510
Sure.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:35.140
So let's start with introductions!

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:37.320
The name's Sawatari.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:38.460
The ability is...

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:41.980
A button?

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:50.750
Behold!

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:53.230
"The ability to turn a button into a rope"!

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:56.690
The hell?

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.420
I said, "The ability to turn—"

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:00.530
Is that for-real your ability?

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:02.690
That blows! It's a freakin' parlor trick!

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:04.240
Oh, shut up!

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:06.700
Tell me somethin' I don't already know!

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:09.620
This guy acts like he's hot stuff, 
but he's total dead weight.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:12.160
Then how's about you, lady?

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:14.250
Don't call me "lady."

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:16.190
I'm Yuuri Amagake.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:19.120
My ability is "the ability to 
quintuple your physical abilities."

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:21.840
That's awesome!

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.310
How's about you, bud?

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:25.340
Madoka Kirisaki.

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:27.510
"The ability to turn a stick into a sword."

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:31.620
Boy, lucky you! You both hit the jackpot!

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:33.040
And you, sir?

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.350
Kumagiri.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:37.680
My ability is apparently to become 
invincible for two seconds.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:38.620
Apparently?

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:41.000
That's what the paper said.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:45.060
But I have no intention of using something 
those people planted in me without my consent!

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:47.790
Are you a professional 
fighter of some kind, sir?

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.950
A professional wrestler... 
on the outside, at least.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.850
Well, good to have ya.

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:55.710
And last but not least...

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:57.980
I'm Akira Shiroyanagi.

00:03:57.980 --> 00:03:58.960
My ability is...

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.720
<i>Should I tell my team my real ability?</i>

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:05.600
<i>The answer: of course not.</i>

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.420
The ability to turn my hand into a cannon.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:10.980
The same one as Cannon Lady?!

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.230
Oh, come on!

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:14.390
Why'm I the only one with an iffy ability?

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:16.750
"Iffy"? More like useless.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:18.440
How'd your one-on-one turn out?

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:22.630
How do you think? 
With an ability like mine...

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:24.760
<i>If I don't tell them my real ability,</i>

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:27.620
<i>I'm locked into whatever 
ability I tell them first.</i>

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:31.660
<i>It's true that if I revealed 
my real ability to my team,</i>

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:34.660
<i>they might be able to help me 
explore its possibilities.</i>

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:40.840
<i>But anyone who knows my ability 
can easily nullify it later.</i>

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:45.270
<i>In other words, revealing my 
ability to the wrong person</i>

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:47.160
<i>could be the death of me.</i>

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:49.730
<i>It's far too risky.</i>

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:54.780
<i>If I am going to tell someone, 
I'll have to choose wisely.</i>

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:59.450
Well, that's introductions out of the way.

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:02.550
How's about we show each 
other what we can d—

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:02.550
Kirisaki.

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:04.650
That reminds me. How's your injury?

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:06.040
What're you talking about?

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:07.590
Hey, that's right!

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:10.150
You two acted like you knew each other.

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:12.680
We fought each other in the one-on-ones.

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:17.430
Oh? The old "enemies one day,
 allies the next"?

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:20.130
And if he's worried about your injuries...

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:23.000
I guess you lost, huh, Kirisaki?

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:23.800
Don't take it too hard!

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.560
Shut your mouth 'fore I murder you!

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:27.340
An' anyway, you lost, too!

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:31.390
They gave me treatment right after.

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:34.300
All just bandages and painkillers, though.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:38.850
Sounds like pretty lousy health care 
for such a tight ship.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:41.230
An indication that they 
consider us expendable.

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:44.440
Who <i>are</i> these guys, anyway?

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:46.350
<i>Good. I managed to change the subject.</i>

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:48.970
I'm less worried about the 
"who" than the "how"...

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:49.300
<i>I really didn't want to have 
to demonstrate my ability.</i>

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:51.530
My last memory before I woke up here was—

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:53.260
<i>There was a chance that it might 
not actually activate here.</i>

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:58.610
<i>The biggest question about my "whatever 
the other person thinks it is" ability...</i>

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:01.810
<i>What does "the other person" indicate?</i>

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:06.210
<i>If it can only mean one's 
obvious enemy in battle,</i>

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:08.800
<i>it wouldn't activate here, 
against my teammates.</i>

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:11.980
<i>A team battle will be my chance to test it,</i>

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:15.710
<i>but the conditions here aren't 
right for experimenting.</i>

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:18.990
<i>In that respect, I'm glad that man's here.</i>

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:22.450
<i>Frivolous enough to reveal 
his ability off the bat,</i>

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:24.490
<i>while naturally falling into 
a "group host" role.</i>

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:26.950
<i>He's taking the attention off of me.</i>

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:30.410
<i>It's almost time.</i>

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:34.850
<i>I'd like to get a grasp of the others' 
abilities and concoct a plan.</i>

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:37.370
Excuse me, Amagake.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:38.480
"Yuuri."

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:41.900
Amagake's an ugly name, and I hate it.

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:43.080
Just call me Yuuri.

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:44.670
O-Okay.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:45.960
Well, Yuuri...

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:48.930
I expect you'll be the key 
to the upcoming battle.

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:52.170
How high can you jump with your ability?

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:53.400
Jump?

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:54.870
Could you show us?

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:56.350
Well, okay...

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:57.240
Just a little one.

00:06:57.510 --> 00:06:58.670
A little one, huh?

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:02.380
<i>Hang on. If she jumps here—</i>

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:09.020
<i>Yeah, called it.</i>

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:12.950
<i>She reached the ceiling effortlessly?
Her ability is—</i>

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:19.010
Y-You tricked me, you stupid perverts!

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:19.160
What the—

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:21.600
I looked away, man.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:23.870
But <i>you</i> looked, you monkeyman freak!

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:25.730
Hey, big guy! Hold him down!

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:28.640
H-Hey, cut it out! We're on the same team!

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:29.110
Shut up, you monkey freak!

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:30.490
Cut it out!

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:36.360
Sheesh. Way to waste your 
energy before the big match.

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:37.440
Oh, shut up!

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:43.010
Look, all I wanted to know was what 
"physical abilities" indicated.

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:46.380
Does it quintuple muscle strength 
without changing your weight?

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:47.750
How does that affect your movements?

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:50.860
A jump seemed like the 
easiest way to test it.

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:52.750
But you looked at my undies.

00:07:52.750 --> 00:07:54.580
I was looking at the <i>jump</i>!

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:58.330
What is it, Pops?

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:00.410
In the upcoming team battle...

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:03.910
If you get your chance, kill your opponent,
 no matter who they are.

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:06.720
Where'd that come from?

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:11.250
Remember what Cannon Lady said at the start?

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:14.380
There's one rule that all 
the programs share...

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:18.550
We're not penalized for killing 
fellow focus group members.

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:25.720
Even the most normal-looking person, 
under the right circumstances, can kill.

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:28.030
I've seen it time and again.

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:30.880
Well, you can write my advice 
off as a joke if you want...

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:34.000
But at least keep your guard up
 if you don't wanna die.

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:35.580
Here we go!

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:42.990
Wow, it's so big!

00:08:42.990 --> 00:08:44.100
It's awfully small...

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:46.150
Is that a ring?

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:49.370
Think I see our opponents.

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:50.490
Four of them?

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:52.600
They're one man short.

00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:55.450
Look! Someone's hiding in the shadows!

00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:57.290
What's his problem?

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:01.140
<i>If that's the ring, does that mean—</i>

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:04.480
<i>The second program will now begin!</i>

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:09.970
<i>The named member from each team will enter 
the ring and fight a one-on-one match.</i>

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:13.410
<i>The results of those matches will 
determine which team is the winner.</i>

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:17.720
<i>Matches can only be resolved 
through expulsion from the ring,</i>

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:20.830
<i>loss of consciousness, admission 
of defeat, or death.</i>

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:23.790
<i>Satoru Sawatari!</i>

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:25.040
<i>Rin Kashii!</i>

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:27.250
<i>Please enter the ring!</i>

00:09:27.470 --> 00:09:28.740
Wait, what?!

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:31.360
The "team matches" ain't 
us fightin' as a team,

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:33.660
but judo-style individual bouts?

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:35.590
<i>They played us for fools.</i>

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:37.460
<i>After the one-on-one matches,</i>

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:40.010
<i>hearing that the next program 
was five-on-five team battles,</i>

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:42.050
<i>and having time to prepare as a group,</i>

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:45.170
<i>encouraged us to reveal our abilities, 
to prepare for the battle ahead.</i>

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:49.700
<i>But a "team battle" that's a 
series of one-on-one bouts</i>

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:52.120
<i>doesn't require us to share our abilities.</i>

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:55.850
<i>We've revealed crucial 
information unnecessarily</i>

00:09:55.850 --> 00:09:58.020
<i>to people we might have 
to fight in the future.</i>

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:02.280
<i>Whoever cooked up this second program</i>

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:04.780
<i>is utterly vicious.</i>

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:07.750
<i>Please begin!</i>

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:12.290
<i>I'm betting there's more 
to this program, too.</i>

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:16.790
<i>She's lookin' pretty low-key...</i>

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:20.180
<i>But I don't trust her one bit!</i>

00:10:23.530 --> 00:10:26.350
Excuse me... Mr. Sawatari, was it?

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:28.720
I have a little favor to ask.

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:33.150
Won't you please forfeit?

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:34.490
What?!

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:42.240
Excuse me... Won't you please forfeit?

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:46.810
I really can't fight another person.

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:50.700
But I'm <i>so</i> afraid of what 
will happen if I lose.

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:54.150
So I was hoping you'd just forfeit.

00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:56.090
Would you, please?

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:58.540
Nice offer, lady.

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:01.430
But I'm betting you got 
somethin' under that sheet.

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:05.560
Or maybe you got an ability 
that uses the cloth somehow.

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:07.320
I know your type.

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:10.360
You get a person's guard down,
and then <i>whammo!</i>

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:13.210
Oh, you've got it all wrong.

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:14.520
I'm wearing this sheet...

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:20.580
Because this is what I came here in.

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:25.250
Of course, I won't ask you 
to forfeit for nothing.

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:28.240
I'd be happy to give you a 
thank-you present after.

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:29.210
Well?

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:31.900
Wh-Wh-What is she talking about?!

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:34.840
<i>I see... you can negotiate like that, too.</i>

00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:38.330
You don't think much of me, do ya?

00:11:38.930 --> 00:11:40.760
But I gotta say...

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:42.050
It ain't a bad offer!

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:44.680
I knew it! Monkey Man is a frickin' perv!

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.780
You suck, dude! I'm gonna kill you!

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:47.490
Don't be stupid!

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:51.690
I meant the part where 
we don't have to fight!

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:55.750
I admit, I'm anything but 
eager to engage in battle.

00:11:55.750 --> 00:11:58.260
My ability's a bit on the dangerous side.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:02.480
If I'm not careful, 
I could end up killing her.

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:06.320
I ain't in the business of harmin' women.

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:09.030
But I also can't just forfeit.

00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:11.740
So how's about we gamble on it?

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:14.750
Whoever loses the flip forfeits on the spot!

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:16.990
Fair and simple, right?

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:21.800
<i>It's true that his ability isn't 
a great one for fighting.</i>

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:25.680
<i>The battle could prove dangerous for him,
 depending on the woman's ability.</i>

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:29.300
<i>So he's bettin' it on a fifty-fifty 
gamble instead, huh?</i>

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:31.300
<i>He's not taking advantage of her?</i>

00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:33.270
<i>Monkey Man's a decent guy after all!</i>

00:12:33.590 --> 00:12:34.750
<i>Wait a minute.</i>

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:36.220
<i>But this strategy...</i>

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:38.310
Very well. I agree.

00:12:38.310 --> 00:12:41.450
I call heads.

00:12:41.450 --> 00:12:43.540
Then I'm tails.

00:12:44.130 --> 00:12:46.070
<i>This is how it's always been for me.</i>

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:47.590
<i>No matter the situation,</i>

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:49.530
<i>no matter what I have to resort to,</i>

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:52.710
<i>I always survive!</i>

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:01.630
So sorry!

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:04.620
I'm just <i>too</i> afraid to forfeit.

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:07.050
So I need you to lose!

00:13:08.590 --> 00:13:11.370
<i>There was one flaw in Sawatari's strategy.</i>

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:16.640
<i>It won't work against someone who 
planned to kill you from the start.</i>

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:19.430
<i>He moved his eyes to the coin,</i>

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:20.910
<i>and that's when she struck.</i>

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:21.860
H-Hey...

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:22.820
Hang on.

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:23.780
Monkey Man?

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:25.590
<i>Calm down.</i>

00:13:25.590 --> 00:13:27.740
<i>Don't stop looking. Don't stop thinking.</i>

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:30.720
<i>What in the hell was her ability?!</i>

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:34.210
Hey, Akira, did you catch it?

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:36.920
I watched the whole thing, 
but I still didn't catch it.

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:41.120
That woman, Rin, barely moved at all.

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:45.260
But those blades appeared out 
of thin air in an instant.

00:13:47.810 --> 00:13:48.750
How's he look?

00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:50.270
Nothing we can do.

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:52.350
All right. Dispose of him.

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:53.400
No way!

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:54.570
Hang on!

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:56.780
Yuuri, keep away from the ring!

00:13:56.780 --> 00:13:58.490
But... dispose of him?

00:13:58.800 --> 00:14:00.410
They can't...

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:02.630
Monkey Man was... just a minute ago...

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:13.790
What a dumbass.

00:14:14.380 --> 00:14:18.670
He acted all cautious, but let his 
guard down when it really mattered.

00:14:19.070 --> 00:14:21.140
If he'd kept his guard up against her,

00:14:21.140 --> 00:14:24.380
we could've figured out 
her ability, at least.

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:25.670
Useless asshole.

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:27.590
H-How can you say that?

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:30.320
How can you say that about 
someone who just died?!

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:32.230
I won't take that lying down, either.

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:35.520
You don't talk that way about a 
comrade who died in the ring.

00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:37.060
Take it back.

00:14:37.740 --> 00:14:38.940
Say that again?

00:14:39.820 --> 00:14:41.100
<i>This isn't good.</i>

00:14:41.450 --> 00:14:44.510
<i>Sawatari's death is affecting 
them more than I expected.</i>

00:14:45.410 --> 00:14:47.660
Looks like a little team 
quarrel over there.

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:50.440
We should really try to keep 
a united front, though!

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:56.450
Does it bother you that I killed someone?

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:57.750
W-Well...

00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:00.950
But don't you remember what we discussed?

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:04.850
He said he had an ability that 
could kill me, remember?

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:08.650
That was the only way I 
could protect myself.

00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:10.320
Right?

00:15:11.060 --> 00:15:13.050
You got a problem, old man?

00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:16.280
<i>I can't afford a team falling-out right now!</i>

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:19.440
They're right.

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:21.700
We're a team, remember?

00:15:21.700 --> 00:15:24.920
And while it's certainly important 
that we speak our minds,

00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:26.970
I don't think now's the time.

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:31.570
I really think we should 
pick this up... later.

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:35.000
I get you...

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:37.010
Later, huh?

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:40.890
<i>Match two:</i>

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:42.570
<i>Shin Kumagiri!</i>

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:44.770
<i>Ringo Tatara!</i>

00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:46.880
<i>Please enter the ring!</i>

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:50.210
Sorry. You're right.

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:52.540
<i>Later, eh?</i>

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:56.300
<i>Indeed, any discussion can wait 
until we've survived this.</i>

00:15:56.520 --> 00:15:59.510
I might be preachin' to 
the choir, old man.

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:05.470
But she seems pretty damn chill about 
the idea of fightin' a hulk like you.

00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:08.160
Don't give us a repeat of Monkey Man.

00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:10.030
I'm aware.

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:12.770
<i>She really does seem extremely calm.</i>

00:16:12.770 --> 00:16:16.300
<i>Is that an indication of a powerful ability?</i>

00:16:16.940 --> 00:16:18.820
<i>But I can't afford to lose!</i>

00:16:19.210 --> 00:16:22.440
<i>Someone needs to put a 
stop this absurd game!</i>

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.020
<i>Please begin, then!</i>

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:27.700
<i>I'm going to learn from Sawatari's example.</i>

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:30.330
<i>I'll get close, while maintaining 
enough distance to react.</i>

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:35.880
<i>If I throw her out of the ring, 
I can win without harming her!</i>

00:16:38.610 --> 00:16:39.590
<i>Here it comes!</i>

00:16:41.320 --> 00:16:42.670
I forfeit.

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:44.940
I admit defeat in this match.

00:16:48.050 --> 00:16:49.100
What in the...

00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:53.300
<i>One fighter has admitted defeat.</i>

00:16:53.730 --> 00:16:56.060
<i>Shin Kumagiri wins.</i>

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:58.200
What the heck?

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:00.820
Maybe her ability's no good in a fight?

00:17:01.130 --> 00:17:02.340
I don't know.

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:05.170
There wasn't enough there to even speculate.

00:17:05.510 --> 00:17:06.990
A bad matchup, maybe?

00:17:07.300 --> 00:17:08.800
I'm sorry.

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:10.890
What happened there, dear?

00:17:11.110 --> 00:17:13.900
There was no way I could beat him.

00:17:14.230 --> 00:17:20.240
I copied his ability, but nothing happened.

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:21.180
Nothing happened?

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:21.850
Yes.

00:17:22.030 --> 00:17:25.660
It must have some kind 
of condition attached.

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:29.210
If I copy an ability and can't 
identify it immediately,

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:31.870
I'm effectively helpless.

00:17:32.240 --> 00:17:35.100
There was no way that I could 
beat a man with his build.

00:17:35.560 --> 00:17:36.760
I see.

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:38.330
Well, you tried your best...

00:17:38.560 --> 00:17:41.020
Is that what you expected to hear?

00:17:41.360 --> 00:17:43.840
You had your opponent on guard for a moment.

00:17:43.840 --> 00:17:47.440
Couldn't you have gotten him 
to show off his ability? Well?

00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:49.910
I think maybe you just weren't trying!

00:17:49.910 --> 00:17:51.670
R-Rin, please!

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:54.240
You <i>do</i> realize this is a 
team match, don't you?

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:58.240
If we lose because of you, 
we might all get penalized.

00:17:58.630 --> 00:18:01.180
Why should I suffer, when I won my match?

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:03.780
Why? Why? Why?!

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:06.300
D-Don't worry, Rin!

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:09.280
My ability gives me a real 
advantage in these fights!

00:18:09.490 --> 00:18:11.310
We'll definitely win the next round!

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:14.240
Oh, right! Good point!

00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:17.110
Sorry I lost my head, you guys!

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:22.510
Thank you for that, Zokumyoin.

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:24.400
It's nothing! We're a team, right?

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:27.370
<i>I'm glad I managed to talk her down.</i>

00:18:27.770 --> 00:18:30.560
<i>But Tatara is also very impressive.</i>

00:18:30.560 --> 00:18:33.790
<i>She didn't show a hint of fear 
while Rin was threatening her.</i>

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:37.090
I was so scared!

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:38.380
What's <i>with</i> that lady?!

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:40.460
Her ability and her personality 
are both terrifying!

00:18:40.460 --> 00:18:42.830
People like that shouldn't be 
allowed to possess deadly weapons!

00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:44.610
<i>Still,</i>

00:18:44.610 --> 00:18:48.060
<i>I definitely couldn't have 
won with my real ability.</i>

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:53.270
<b><<Plagiarist>>

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:53.280
<i>My ability to copy another person's 
ability at one-tenth values...</i>

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:59.230
<i>In practice, when I activate it, I can view 
the ability of the person I'm copying.</i>

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:00.200
<b>Become invincible 
for 2 seconds</b>

00:19:00.940 --> 00:19:04.030
<i>The internal haiku of Ringo Tatara:</i>

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:07.820
<i>"Copy his power - and a mere point-two seconds
 - is all that you get."</i>

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:07.960
Copy his power
And a mere point-two seconds
Is all that you get

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:09.680
<i>No way is that happening!</i>

00:19:10.130 --> 00:19:11.510
I forfeit!

00:19:12.180 --> 00:19:14.350
<i>I'm so glad that surrender was an option!</i>

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:16.460
<i>Match three.</i>

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:17.540
<i>Madoka Kirisaki!</i>

00:19:17.890 --> 00:19:19.670
<i>Saeko Zokumyoin!</i>

00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:21.510
<i>Please enter the ring!</i>

00:19:21.730 --> 00:19:23.770
Looks pretty scrawny to me.

00:19:23.770 --> 00:19:25.690
Don't let your guard down, Kirisaki.

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:27.970
Zokumyoin...

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:29.430
Remember your promise.

00:19:32.720 --> 00:19:34.690
<i>Now, please begin!</i>

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:39.400
<i>It'd be hard to dive into sword range 
with my hands bound like this.</i>

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:42.130
<i>And I should probably keep 
my distance at first.</i>

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:46.530
A slingshot?

00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:51.690
If I can strike first, I win!

00:20:00.330 --> 00:20:04.540
An ability that turns marbles into 
big ol' wrecking balls, huh?

00:20:05.050 --> 00:20:07.540
Good thing I swiped it away just in case...

00:20:09.320 --> 00:20:10.350
Not bad!

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:11.480
<i>Marbles?</i>

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:13.680
<i>He was able to see it in that instant?</i>

00:20:14.090 --> 00:20:17.790
<i>He's got some serious kinetic 
vision and reflexes.</i>

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:22.360
I didn't expect to fight 
someone so competent.

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:26.260
Woulda turned out pretty bad 
if that'd hit me head-on.

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:27.710
But if you wanna play rough...

00:20:28.070 --> 00:20:30.140
I'm free to play rough, too!

00:20:32.880 --> 00:20:34.360
<i>He turned his stick into a sword!</i>

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:36.840
Now it's my turn, girlie!

00:20:37.060 --> 00:20:40.840
<i>I'll need to enlarge it 
before he bats it away!</i>

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:45.140
H-He's so fast!

00:20:45.140 --> 00:20:47.350
You think I couldn't see 
what you were thinkin'?

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:50.100
Then I'll try three at once!

00:20:54.640 --> 00:20:56.200
And one more!

00:20:57.220 --> 00:20:58.190
Kirisaki!

00:21:04.170 --> 00:21:06.230
Not bad at all.

00:21:06.480 --> 00:21:08.460
You had a pretty good idea there.

00:21:08.460 --> 00:21:11.410
Incredible. He cut it in half.

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:15.860
<i>I'll bet Akira's caught on by now.</i>

00:21:15.860 --> 00:21:16.710
<i>Yeah...</i>

00:21:16.990 --> 00:21:19.510
<i>My real ability is...</i>

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:25.060
<i>The ability to turn a stick into a 
sword </i>that can cut through anything<i>!</i>

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:25.470
<b><<Trueblade>>

00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:28.320
I... I have to fight someone like this?

00:21:31.190 --> 00:21:33.200
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:40.020
<b><<Trueblade>>

00:23:10.280 --> 00:23:13.280
<b>Mion and Yang's 
\h\h\hNext Episode Preview</b>

00:23:10.890 --> 00:23:13.450
Mion and Yang's Next Episode Preview!

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:17.320
Did you enjoy the third episode 
of <i>Battle Game in 5 Seconds</i>?

00:23:17.630 --> 00:23:19.980
Miss Mion! It's time for the preview!

00:23:19.980 --> 00:23:21.260
What are you doing?

00:23:21.260 --> 00:23:23.060
Well, I had no screen time this episode!

00:23:23.060 --> 00:23:25.660
I thought I'd sing the opening next time!

00:23:25.660 --> 00:23:29.160
Next time: Beautiful Prodigy 
Singer Mion makes her debut!

00:23:29.160 --> 00:23:31.460
W-Wait a minute! You can't do that!

00:23:31.460 --> 00:23:32.520
You just can't!

00:23:32.520 --> 00:23:33.610
How come?

00:23:33.610 --> 00:23:35.680
Why are you so desperate to stop me?

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:38.160
You just can't!

00:23:38.160 --> 00:23:39.710
Hey, you're a good singer.
